   "daf": "6a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "הַצַּד הַשָּׁוֶה שֶׁבָּהֶן. לְאֵתוֹיֵי מַאי? אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: לְאֵתוֹיֵי אַבְנוֹ סַכִּינוֹ וּמַשָּׂאוֹ שֶׁהִנִּיחָן בְּרֹאשׁ גַּגּוֹ, וְנָפְלוּ בְּרוּחַ מְצוּיָה וְהִזִּיקוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «The common denominator of» the components in all these categories is that it is their typical manner to cause damage. The Gemara asks: In order «to add what» halakha is this statement cited in the mishna? «Abaye said:» The stating of the common denominator in the mishna serves «to add» that one is liable in a case of «his stone, his knife, or his load, where he placed them on top of his roof, and they fell» off the roof «by means of a common wind and caused damage.»"
  }
